research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-616153-+     "id": "derive-4-1",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:616154:+     "claim": "The exceptional branch of $G$ is never taken, and $g$ is strictly increasing and cofinal: both branches of $G$ take values in $\\alpha$, so $g[\\xi] \\subseteq \\alpha$ for every $\\xi \\in \\beta_0$; and $g \\restriction \\xi$ is a map $\\xi \\to \\alpha$ with $\\xi \\in \\beta_0$, so its range is **not** cofinal by the minimality of step 2.1, whence [L1] supplies $\\zeta \\in \\alpha$ with $g(\\eta) < \\zeta$ for every $\\eta \\in \\xi$, so $g(\\eta) \\cup \\{g(\\eta)\\} \\le \\zeta$ and $\\sup\\{\\,g(\\eta) \\cup \\{g(\\eta)\\} : \\eta \\in \\xi\\,\\} \\le \\zeta \\in \\alpha$ by [L2] and [L3]; that supremum therefore lies in $\\alpha$, the first branch applies, and $g(\\eta) \\in g(\\eta) \\cup \\{g(\\eta)\\} \\subseteq g(\\xi)$ gives $g(\\eta) \\in g(\\xi)$ for every $\\eta \\in \\xi$; finally $f(\\xi) \\subseteq g(\\xi)$ for every $\\xi$, so $g$ is cofinal because $f$ is, which is claim (b). [step 2.1, step 3.1, L1, L2, L3, L5]",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-616155-+     "step": "4.1",
